PHASE 4 — ADVANCED PRODUCT VARIANT ENGINE
==================================================

Implement a proper Product Variant Management System.

Understand the difference between:

- Product Attributes: Technical or descriptive product information.
- Product Variants: Purchasable versions of the same product.
- Product Options: Choices presented to customers.
- Product Specifications: Structured technical information.
- Product Features: Highlighted selling points.
- Product Custom Fields: Additional administrator-defined information.

These concepts must be implemented separately but integrated correctly.

Examples:

MOBILE PHONE:

Product: Samsung Galaxy

Variant dimensions:
- RAM: 8GB / 12GB
- Storage: 128GB / 256GB / 512GB
- Color: Black / Blue / Silver

Each valid variant may have its own:

- SKU
- Price
- Sale Price
- Stock Quantity
- Images
- Availability
- Barcode
- Weight
- Status

SHIRT:

Variant dimensions:
- Size: S / M / L / XL / XXL
- Color: Black / White / Blue

SHOES:

Variant dimensions:
- Size: 38 / 39 / 40 / 41 / 42 / 43 / 44 / 45
- Color
- Material where relevant

The administrator must be able to:

1. Create custom variant dimensions.
2. Add unlimited practical option values.
3. Create combinations of options.
4. Generate valid variant combinations.
5. Exclude unavailable combinations.
6. Set individual variant prices.
7. Set individual variant stock.
8. Set individual variant SKUs.
9. Upload variant-specific images.
10. Enable or disable individual variants.
11. Edit or delete variants.
12. Manage variant availability.
13. Track inventory independently per variant.

Do not assume every product needs variants.

A simple product must be creatable without variants.

Do not generate unnecessary combinations or duplicate SKUs.

Ensure inventory is updated correctly when a customer purchases a specific variant.

